 "context": "<div data-type=\"note\" data-has-label=\"true\" id=\"fs-id1986955\" class=\"interactive ost-tag-lo-apbio-ch06-s05-aplo-4-17 ost-tag-lo-apbio-ch06-s05-lo02 ost-assessed-feature\" data-label=\"Link to Learning\">\n<h2 class=\"os-title\" data-type=\"title\">\n  <span class=\"os-title-label\">Link to Learning</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"os-note-body\">\n<p id=\"fs-id2065566\">View an animation of induced fit at <a href=\"https://openstax.org/l/hexokinase\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\">this website</a>.\n</p>\n<div data-type=\"injected-exercise\" class=\"os-embed autogenerated-content\" data-injected-from-nickname=\"\" data-injected-from-version=\"17\" data-injected-from-url=\"https://exercises.openstax.org/api/exercises?q=tag:apbio-ch06-ex056\" data-tags=\"apbio-ch06 apbio-ch06-s05 apbio-ch06-s05-lo01 apbio-ch06-ex056 context-cnxmod:b58b6923-aad7-4c62-907e-fb0c0ba08f44 exid:apbio-ch06-ex056 context-cnxfeature:fs-id1986955 context-cnxmod:1dc8fdc5-8378-46b7-9bf0-013313899fa3 context-cnxmod:99b98703-3f88-4b35-88f9-9f53c7cc614d context-cnxmod:2d231f13-8996-4207-9a3e-5daba9aa7edc aplo:stax-apbio:ENE-1.E interactive dok:2 aplo:stax-apbio:ENE-1.L filter-type:import:has-context time:short blooms:3 assignment-type:homework science-practice:argumentation book:stax-bio apbio book:stax-apbio filter-type:import:hs inbook-yes book-slug:biology-ap-courses module-slug:biology:7-2-glycolysis module-slug:biology-2e:7-2-glycolysis module-slug:biology-ap-courses:6-5-enzymes module-slug:biology-ap-courses:7-2-glycolysis time:medium book-slug:biology book-slug:biology-2e assessment:preparedness:https://openstax.org/orn/book:page/8d50a0af-948b-4204-a71d-4826cba765b8:1dc8fdc5-8378-46b7-9bf0-013313899fa3\" data-is-vocab=\"false\" data-question-count=\"1\" data-is-multipart=\"False\">\n    \n    <div data-type=\"exercise-question\" data-is-answer-order-important=\"true\" data-formats=\"free-response multiple-choice\" id=\"334273\"><div class=\"os-problem-container\">\n        <div data-type=\"question-stem\">Phosphofructokinase (PFK) deficiency is a genetic disorder that occurs when a person lacks PFK, an enzyme needed to perform glycolysis in skeletal muscles. Apply your understanding of both enzyme function and glycolysis to predict the effect that PFK deficiency could have on the body.</div>\n        <ol data-type=\"question-answers\" type=\"a\">\n            <li data-type=\"question-answer\" data-correctness=\"\">\n                <div data-type=\"answer-content\">Production of energy by glycolysis will occur more slowly than normal; skeletal muscles will function properly.</div>\n                \n            </li>\n            <li data-type=\"question-answer\" data-correctness=\"\">\n                <div data-type=\"answer-content\">Production of energy by glycolysis will not occur; skeletal muscles will function properly.</div>\n                \n            </li>\n            <li data-type=\"question-answer\" data-correctness=\"\">\n                <div data-type=\"answer-content\">Production of energy by glycolysis will occur more erratically than normal; skeletal muscles will not function properly.</div>\n                \n            </li>\n            <li data-type=\"question-answer\" data-correctness=\"\">\n                <div data-type=\"answer-content\">Production of energy by glycolysis will not occur; skeletal muscles will not function properly.</div>\n                \n            </li>\n            </ol>\n        </div></div>\n    </div>\n</div>\n</div>",
 "stimulus_html": "",
